    <bpmn:process id="W_W4782" name="W4782. OCPI Roaming, eMSP Integration &amp; Cross-Network Interoperability" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Network launch; eMSP roaming partnership; CPO interoperability
Frequency: Per partnership + continuous
Volume: ~3–6 roaming partners/eMSPs for cross-network access
Owner: EV Program Manager / IT (VS-27) / Finance (VS-80)
Participants: eMSP/roaming-hub partners, Finance (VS-80), IT (VS-27)
Source: workflow W4782 — OCPI Roaming, eMSP Integration &amp; Cross-Network Interoperability</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4782_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4782_Lane1" name="IT">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4782_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4782_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4782_Lane2" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4782_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4782_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4782_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4782_Start4" name="Network launch; eMSP roaming partnership; CPO interoperability">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4782_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4782_Task5" name="Implement OCPI (Open Charge Point Interface) roaming: expose BuildRight charge…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Implement OCPI (Open Charge Point Interface) roaming: expose BuildRight charge points to roaming hubs/eMSPs (so any EV driver&#x27;s app/card works), consume external networks where useful, and manage the cdr (charge-detail-record) exchange; this maximizes utilization by removing &quot;wrong-app&quot; friction
Responsible (R): IT / EV Program / CPO
Accountable (A): EV Program Manager / CIO
Duration: Per partnership</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4782_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4782_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4782_Task6" name="Negotiate and contract roaming/eMSP partnerships: revenue-share/clearing terms…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Negotiate and contract roaming/eMSP partnerships: revenue-share/clearing terms, branding, SLA, and data-sharing (RA 10173 VS-91); manage the CDR clearing/settlement (links VS-80 payment settlement) and reconciliation
Responsible (R): Finance / Legal / IT / EV Program
Accountable (A): EV Program Manager / Finance
Duration: Per partnership</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4782_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4782_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4782_Task7" name="Operate and reconcile roaming: monitor cross-network session success, settle…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Operate and reconcile roaming: monitor cross-network session success, settle CDR-based revenue-share monthly, manage disputes/failed-CDRs, and report roaming contribution to analytics (W4792); ensure tariff transparency across networks (Consumer Act W469)
Responsible (R): Finance / IT / EV Program
Accountable (A): EV Program Manager / Finance
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4782_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4782_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4782_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4782_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-720 (ensure controlled execution — Station Deployment, Energy Integration &amp; Roaming/Payment (PA-163.2).) | - CTL-720: OCPI roaming enabled; CDRs validated &amp; reconciled; tariff transparent; DPAs in place (VS-91)
Owner: EV Program Manager / IT (VS-27) / Finance (VS-80)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
