    <bpmn:process id="W_W4784" name="W4784. Go-Live Readiness, Site Acceptance &amp; Hypercare Handover" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Commissioning complete (W4778/W4781); site about to go live
Frequency: Per site
Volume: ~each site at launch
Owner: EV Program Manager / PMO (VS-112) / Facilities (VS-138)
Participants: Facilities, IT (VS-27), OCM (VS-134), Store Ops (VS-07), CPO
Source: workflow W4784 — Go-Live Readiness, Site Acceptance &amp; Hypercare Handover</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4784_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4784_Lane1" name="EV Program">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4784_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4784_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4784_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4784_Lane2" name="OCM">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4784_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4784_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4784_Start4" name="Commissioning complete (W4778/W4781); site about to go live">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4784_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4784_Task5" name="Run the go-live readiness &amp; site-acceptance test (SAT): end-to-end test (access…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Run the go-live readiness &amp; site-acceptance test (SAT): end-to-end test (access → charge → bill → notify → idle-fee), safety checks (emergency-stop, GFCI, signage), accessibility (PWD bays), tariff display (Consumer Act W469), OCPP/OCPI/CSMS health, and store-team readiness; obtain sign-off before public launch
Responsible (R): EV Program / Facilities / IT / OCM
Accountable (A): EV Program Manager
Duration: Per site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4784_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4784_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4784_Task6" name="Train the store team (VS-134 OCM): basic customer assistance (&quot;how to start a…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Train the store team (VS-134 OCM): basic customer assistance (&quot;how to start a charge&quot;), escalation path for faults (W4789), safety/emergency response, and the basket-offer script (W4773); brief on PWD assistance and the dwell-offer
Responsible (R): OCM / Store Ops / EV Program
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Per site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4784_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4784_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4784_Task7" name="Enter hypercare: intensified monitoring (uptime, faults, session success) for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Enter hypercare: intensified monitoring (uptime, faults, session success) for the first weeks, rapid-issue resolution with the CPO/vendor, and the transition to steady-state operations (W4789) once stable; capture lessons for the next site (VS-133)
Responsible (R): EV Program / IT / CPO
Accountable (A): EV Program Manager
Duration: Per site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4784_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4784_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4784_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4784_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-720 (ensure controlled execution — Station Deployment, Energy Integration &amp; Roaming/Payment (PA-163.2).) | - CTL-720: SAT passed before public launch; store team trained (VS-134); hypercare exited only on stability criteria
Owner: EV Program Manager / PMO (VS-112) / Facilities (VS-138)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
